ngly huge park area sort of around  the city center and a lot of space which  I wouldn't do anything with and I was  really figuring it would be kind of  awkward to have that around the Central  Station there but this is also something  which I'm definitely up for feedback to  as well because I'm still not sure if I  really want to keep the houses over here  the idea was basically to just at least  make this area a bit more dense and make  the housing developments over here fit  in with the houses which I already have  on the other side of this road and give  that sort of modern suburban style to it  which even though I'm quite happy with  how this small development came out and  it's really inspired by the really small  developments which are very newly  planned around cities I'm not quite sure  if the placement around here is really  the best and yet I also feel like if I'm  in place this housing development here  I'm not sure what else I would really  place here so I'm really on the fence  about this area regardless of that  though this is what it look like at the  moment and this is what it looked like  at the moment which is just some simple  houses very large gardens and very large  houses as well and just wanted to make  this really one of those more modern and  spaced out housing developments but  still I'm very unsure about the  placement and not to mention that it's  of course it's awkward it's awkward ly  close to the city centre as well but  also it sort of is just underneath that  main road over there and very close to  the canal as well so it even though it  looks sort of spaced out it really has  an awkward placement in the city and the  general issue I guess really boils down  to if I keep this place empty it feels  like too large of an empty field to keep  in the park or keeping the city and if I  make it a park it would really feel like  there are too many parks in this area  yet to keep it as a little neighborhood  with houses it would feel like it's a  little bit too forced and too small  - oddly placed over here so I'm really  not entirely sure what I really want to  do with that here so that's I guess why  I would be up for feedback I am in the  end still quite happy with how it looks  it's do something which I'm not sure if  I really want to place it in the city  like this and now I just wanted to very  quickly add some more foliage to at  least make that a little bit nicer  around the city but the main thing which  I'll actually be doing in the remainder  of this episode is get the road textures  done which is something which I really  wanted to try which I haven't tried up  to this point is to just replace all the  roads with gravel roads to make sure  that they're all flat and actually put  my own textures over them or at least  particulars over them manually which is  something which I really wanted to try  because having the asphalt roads is just  something which is quite rare in the  Netherlands anyway when it comes to the  three types of roads in the Netherlands  and you have the roads that are used  within neighborhoods and for people to  get to run their houses they are barely  if at all asphalt roads and really one  of my main issues with the city as a  whole is also that it uses so many  asphalt roads because there is barely  any other way except for while doing  this manually for every single part of  the city but also just because  especially when it comes to city centres  the colour and tacky of the roads really  makes a really huge difference to how  the city overall looks and so I really  wanted to try and get some more fancy  bricks textures in here not you not just  to make it look a little bit more  traditional and old-fashioned but also  to get it to look a little bit better as  well and it also allows for a couple of  those fun things which often Dutch roads  do and the other parts of town of in the  older parts of towns where where  different roads meet up there'd be  planters or a 